module v2.test.claim.manual.annotation_gap_v1_v2_agreement_probe_pair

import std.types { CommitSha, String, commit_sha_text_holds }

// THE PROBE PAIR THAT SHOWS THE AGREEMENT CONTROL IS NOT VACUOUS, recorded as data rather than as prose
// a reader has to trust. The fields are the receipt: kind, the ref the red tree is durable on, the main
// commit it was cut from, the two commits where the control was OBSERVED failing and passing, and the
// date it was executed.
//
// WHY A DELIBERATE BREAK RATHER THAN A BEFORE/AFTER FEATURE TEST. The row this node closes says the
// "gated agreement control turns red" when the v2 roster drops infix applications as regions. The control
// is called that here because the row calls it so; it is NOT enrolled in any gated row -- the admission was
// held -- so this red witness is carried by its executions alone, in the runs pinned on the pull request.
// That red
// cannot exist on any main commit -- on main the roster is whole -- so the only honest witness of it is
// a tree where the arm was removed by hand. `kind` records that: red_at is NOT a claim that main is
// broken, it is evidence the control is not vacuous. The arm is the second disjunct of
// v2.compiler.parse parse_node_is_source_region (the infix-application projection); drop it and a
// comment before `2 * 3` loses `2 * 3` as its neighbour on the v2 side while v1 still names it, so the
// fixture row "before the product" in v2.test.claim.manual.annotation_gap_v1_v2_agreement -- the row the
// control gained for exactly this reason, the four rows before it contain no infix application and could
// not see the break -- disagrees and the claim fails.
//
// `git diff <red_at>^ <red_at>` is the break and nothing else. green_at is a real commit on the PR
// lineage, and the witness file is BYTE-IDENTICAL between red_at and green_at -- only the roster differs
// -- which is what makes the pair a mutation control rather than two different tests.
// RE-CUT, NAMED. The first pair (red_at 1013d02dace7f8a95ac78a10fc1bcbbc46488a5c, green_at
// 5b84464bb27acbe00542b35ef008b808a7712aa0) WAS executed, and the control refused to resolve there:
// closure-strict-resolve reported "function 'nth' not found in scope" at the fifth row's assertion, exit
// 1 -- a defect in this branch's own fixture edit, invisible until something ran the file, which nothing
// had, because it lives under manual/. The pair was re-cut at the head carrying the fixed accessor; the
// old break commit is not lost, because the durable ref's history keeps it as an ancestor of the new one.
// RE-CUT AGAIN, NAMED. The second pair (red_at c65a78eec60b9b8c9a458b59c0230a96278b327b, green_at
// 74e3818cadf75413242bbff9bd138a0851f4b504) WAS executed with the same main-built binary, and the control
// again refused to resolve: the effect checker reported "effect summary incomplete: call to
// 'dag_language_model' ... has no established callee identity" and the same for 'span_index_extent', exit 1
// -- two callees the control has called bare since it was written, with no top-level import, another defect
// nothing under manual/ had ever exposed. Both are imported now (7a6fd7924b0e8cec3988628eb129cad1e4a545e8),
// which is green_at below; that commit's first parent is the head the refusal was observed at, so the pair
// moved forward one fix rather than sideways. Both earlier break commits stay reachable: the durable ref's
// newest commit carries the previous one as a second parent, so no break is rewritten away -- read
// `git log <probe_ref>` to see all three.
// RE-CUT A THIRD TIME, NAMED, AND IT FAILED -- FOR A DIFFERENT REASON, RECORDED RATHER THAN RE-ROLLED. The
// third pair (red_at fd8fc90a048581364791b970cda34b224d7089cc, green_at 7a6fd7924b0e8cec3988628eb129cad1e4a545e8,
// round E2) executed cleanly on both sides and BOTH printed PASS with exit status 0. That is a failed pair, not a
// passed one: a control that also passes on the tree where the roster arm was removed is INSENSITIVE to the plant,
// and the row demands it go red. It is recorded here with both PASS lines and both rc values rather than re-rolled
// until it cooperated. The cause was in the fixture, not the harness: the fifth row's comment sat before the WHOLE
// expression `1 + 2 * 3`, so the neighbour it names was a region that exists with or without the arm. The carrier
// says so at main -- src/v2/compiler/parse.dag:142-149, untouched by this PR: "Without the second, `1 + 2 * 3`
// would have no region for `2 * 3`, and a comment before it would get `2` as its neighbour." So the arm is only
// observable from a gap INSIDE the application. The fixture moved (08b009527e8fca04e87f819dee18708946cfcc41): the
// comment now sits after the '+', and two after-only pipelines PIN the neighbour text each parser names for that
// gap to the literal `2 * 3` -- an agreement conjunct alone cannot catch two parsers agreeing on the WRONG
// neighbour, which is exactly what the third pair did. The expectation's authority is that quoted fixture text and
// that main-line comment, NOT any parser output: a scratch candidate-set drift detector (untracked file
// src/v2/test/manual/zqx_agreement_probe.dag, never landed, outside the pair property) was run at both trees to
// show per side which candidate each parser takes, and its table is pasted in the log beside the pair.
// red_at below is that break re-cut on top of the fixture commit (first parent green_at, second parent the
// previous break so no break commit is ever deleted); green_at is the fixture commit itself, where the control was
// executed and passed. Earlier superseded pairs: first pair red_at 1013d02dace7f8a95ac78a10fc1bcbbc46488a5c /
// green_at 5b84464bb27acbe00542b35ef008b808a7712aa0 (the witness could not resolve at all -- bare `fold`,
// `dag_language_model`, missing span_index_extent); second pair red_at c65a78ee18095a84215585382773205859d62a44 /
// green_at fd8fc90a048581364791b970cda34b224d7089cc (resolved, but that tree's witness was pre-fixture-change).

// THE LABELS THAT WERE DATA, AND WHY THEY ARE NOT. An earlier revision published kind, the durable ref, the
// executed-on date, the witness module and fn, the roster arm, the two-root refusal and the argv roots as
// `data` rows beside the SHAs. Nothing read them -- eight rows with one reference each, their own declaration
// -- and a claim that no predicate consumes is commentary wearing a type, which
// gunbc.design_argument::guarantee_ladder (rung honesty) ranks below simply writing it in prose. They are
// prose now, in full. Only the three SHAs stay data, because those three and only those are consumed, by
// `probe_pair_receipt_shas_are_real_commit_shas` below.
//   kind: deliberate-break.  durable ref: refs/heads/red-control/parse-comment-gap-attachment-v2-consumed
//   witness: v2.test.claim.manual.annotation_gap_v1_v2_agreement, fn v1_and_v2_agree_on_neighbour_text_holds
//   arm removed in red_at: the second disjunct of v2.compiler.parse parse_node_is_source_region,
//     `|| parse_node_has_authored_edge(name: ^grammar_infix_left_node_projection)`
//   executed on: 2026-11-23 for the pair, re-executed 2026-11-24 once this receipt itself was edited; the raw
//     PASS/FAIL lines and each command's real exit status live in the run log pinned on PR gunb-ai/gunbc#16942
//   argv roots: dag, src/v1, src/v2 -- two roots refuse this control's v1 imports at the checker
data annotation_gap_v1_v2_agreement_probe_red_base: CommitSha = "8c86ee47f68ec1f451e25a8cb8f594a868e5c384"
// red_at's FIRST PARENT is green_at: the break is one commit on top of the tree whose witness it runs
// unchanged, which is the strictest form of the pair -- the two runs differ by the roster arm alone.
data annotation_gap_v1_v2_agreement_probe_red_at: CommitSha = "ca2a086a1e69699aa95c0103a89b370a4127c447"
// green_at is the commit the control was EXECUTED at and PASSED, on this PR lineage. The head carrying this receipt
// is green_at plus one commit that touches only this receipt module, so the witness bytes are the same in
// green_at, in the head, and in red_at (proven by git hash-object in the run log).
data annotation_gap_v1_v2_agreement_probe_green_at: CommitSha = "08b009527e8fca04e87f819dee18708946cfcc41"
// HOW THIS CONTROL IS EXECUTED, recorded because the instrument is not the obvious one, and a reader who
// reaches for the floor's own two-root command will otherwise find the control unrunnable and conclude the
// wrong thing. claim_batch with the floor's CLI roots (--source-root dag --source-root src/v2) cannot
// resolve this control's imports: it refuses at the checker with "unresolved import: module
// 'v1.compiler.tokenize' not found" (and likewise v1.compiler.parse, v1.compiler.annotation_bind,
// v1.std.core) -- observed at tree d7de0f06938f5f072bc3a3b5c8c9ea0fffa343fd with a claim_batch built from
// main 8c86ee47f68ec1f451e25a8cb8f594a868e5c384, exit status 1. src/v1 is not a root the floor can carry
// (src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run.rs records widening the roots as ruled out: src/v1 and src/v2 collide on
// twelve last segments, so a shared pool re-binds bare cross-module references), and the same refusal
// falls on the precedent v2.test.claim.parse.data_initializer_layout_parse, which imports three of those
// v1 modules and is listed as a gated row. MEASURED 2026-11-24, STRUCTURALLY: nothing in that floor runs.
// `grep -rn "fn run_required_floor" src/v1/stage0/src --include=*.rs` returns nothing; the only reader of
// the decoded selector rosters is a peak-bytes instrument (src/v1/stage0/src/target_invocation_host.rs:3483,
// dispatched :751, registered at src/v1/stage0/src/instrument_registry_generated.rs:50); and 0 of the 9
// files under .github/workflows passes any --required flag. A listed row is therefore a green no executor
// produces, which is why this control was not enrolled to gain a second one beside
// dag/test/claim/v1_dag_parse_witness.dag -- a gated prefix row whose claim calls run_v1_dag_parse() without
// importing it, so no executor can run it either. The pair was executed with three named roots under
// claim_batch, one argv on both trees, and those runs are the whole of its evidence; no gate runs it.
// The refusal text itself is the evidence and it lives VERBATIM in the run log (round B, block A1: the
// four unresolved-import lines with the command, the tree and the real exit status 1). Those two recorded
// facts are POINTERS into that log, not proofs of it -- a Bool in a witness cannot certify an observation
// made outside itself, which is why the two-root refusal and the argv roots are prose now rather than rows,
// and CommitSha here is an unvalidated String alias (dag/std/types.dag:201, whose own
// comment says the predicate beside it is a check a caller must remember to run, not a construction wall).
// What the log anchors: the tree sha named in the comment above is proved to exist as a commit by
// 'git cat-file -e <sha>^{commit}' with its own exit status, and the binary that produced the refusal is
// hashed by a verbatim 'sha256sum' line. No binary hash is recorded in this module, because no predicate
// in the language would fail against a fabricated one -- the hash belongs in the log beside the run that
// produced it, which is where it is.

// WHY A CLAIM AND NOT A REVIEWER. CommitSha is an unvalidated String alias (dag/std/types.dag:201), and
// its comment says so: the predicate beside it is a validating CHECK a caller must remember to run, not a
// construction wall. A field holding a placeholder therefore parses, typechecks and passes CI as a receipt
// that looks complete -- which is a fiction that merges. Running this claim refuses that: any value that is
// not forty lowercase hex characters fails it, so an unfilled placeholder cannot survive an executed run.
// test.claim.std_commit_sha_text_witness is the oracle for the predicate itself; this claim is a CONSUMER
// of it, refusing on the three fields this receipt publishes.
test fn probe_pair_receipt_shas_are_real_commit_shas() -> Bool {
  commit_sha_text_holds(head: annotation_gap_v1_v2_agreement_probe_red_base)
    && commit_sha_text_holds(head: annotation_gap_v1_v2_agreement_probe_red_at)
    && commit_sha_text_holds(head: annotation_gap_v1_v2_agreement_probe_green_at)
}
